meta {
  name: Import Master Data from Tenant
  type: http
  seq: 11
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/master-data/branch/import-from-tenant
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{businessAccessToken}}
}

docs {
  The branch-admin "Import Master Data" action: sync the tenant's **Tenant Master
  Data → the active branch's Branch Master Data** (full overwrite of tests +
  panels). Requires a branch-scoped token (`active_branch_id` from the JWT) — 400
  otherwise.

  Update-or-create keyed on provenance (`sourceMasterLabTestId` /
  `sourceMasterLabPanelId`, falling back to test/panel code): existing branch rows
  are fully overwritten from the tenant catalogue, missing ones are created, no
  duplicates. Panel membership is remapped to the branch test copies. Runs as one
  transaction. Hand-created branch rows can't exist (branch admins can't create).
  Returns `{ tests: { created, updated }, panels: { created, updated } }`.

  **Authorization:** requires ANY of `branch_admin:master_data__import_master_lab_tests`
  or `branch_admin:master_data__import_master_lab_panels` (one atomic import covers
  both). `branch_admin` holds both by baseline; `business_admin`/`administrator`
  bypass. A branch role missing both → 403 PERMISSION_DENIED.

  **TAT propagation:** after the sync, each updated branch test/panel's TAT is
  carried into its Lab Test List / Lab Panel List copies in **every** list of the
  branch (user duplicates excluded) — the rows Create Order's Diagnostic Items and
  the TAT engine read — so a TAT configured in Tenant Master Data no longer needs a
  manual per-list "Sync from Master Data". A copy is updated only when its TAT is
  empty or still equals the previous master TAT; branch-customised TAT is kept.
  Re-running this import also fills copies that were left without TAT earlier.
}
